    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both of its tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to the new spec. All changes are in `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`:\n\n**New `Soundex.java`** \u2014 standard American Soundex encoding of a surname (first letter + three digits, e.g. `R163`), used as the phonetic component of both the identity key and the soft-match rule. Handles null/blank/letter-free names by returning `\"\"`.\n\n**`IdentityKey.java`** \u2014 now returns `sha256Hex(normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName))`, a 64-char lowercase hex string. The telephone still normalizes to E.164 (verbatim fallback), the email lowercases (empty when absent). **`householdId` is no longer part of the key.**\n\n**`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** \u2014 logic unchanged (it keys on `IdentityKey.of`), so 409 now fires on the new key, still skipping soft-deleted owners. The email-domain blocklist (`RejectDisposableEmailDomain`) already runs earlier in the POST pipeline, so it still applies first. Since `householdId` dropped out of the key, the separate household-duplicate 409 no longer applies \u2014 two owners with the same surname/postcode but different telephones now have distinct keys.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 soft match now triggers when `IdentityKey.of` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode both match an existing (non-deleted) owner, picking the lowest matching id. This is what those same-surname/same-postcode/different-telephone owners now become instead of a hard 409. `sharesHousehold` and missing-postcode short-circuits are preserved.\n\nI also updated the doc comments in `EnsureUniqueIdentity`, `FlagPossibleDuplicate`, and the two step comments in `owners.POST.yml` to describe the new behaviour.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (409 on identical identity) both green.",
